     "Liolaemus goetschi is a species of lizard in the family  Liolaemidae. It is endemic to Argentina."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Etymology",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The specific name, goetschi, is in honor of Wilhelm Goetsch, who was a German herpetologist and entomologist."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Geographic range",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "L. goetschi is found in the Argentinian provinces of Neuquén and Río Negro."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Habitat",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The preferred natural habitats of L. goetschi are grassland and shrubland, at altitudes of 300–700 m (980–2,300 ft)."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Description",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "L. goetschi may attain a snout-to-vent length (SVL) of about 7.5 cm (3.0 in). It has a patch of enlarged scales on the posterior surface of the femur."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Diet",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "L. goetschi is omnivorous."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Reproduction",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "L. goetschi is oviparous."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Taxonomy",
